# Flutter Monorepo Standards

Read `AGENTS.md` and `DESIGN.md` before writing any code.

Detailed rules are split across companion files in `.cursor/rules/`:

| File | Covers |
|---|---|
| `monorepo_architecture.mdc` | Repo structure, must-use packages, import rules, Melos |
| `design_system.mdc` | Theme, spacing, radii, responsive layout, shared widgets |
| `logging_and_errors.mdc` | AppLogger usage, Result<T>, error boundaries |
| `testing_and_commits.mdc` | Test structure, pre-commit checks, commit format |

Quick rules:
- Never `print()`. Use `AppLogger`.
- Never hardcode colors/sizes. Use `Theme.of(context)` and `AppSpacing`/`AppRadius`.
- Always import from `package:foo/foo.dart`, never from `package:foo/src/...`.
- Extend shared packages rather than duplicating logic in apps.
